Z||000009||sluppy123||07-29-2001||12:08 PM||||All right I'll try to answer all your questions. <BR>Smooth-No I don't plan to run n2o with the turbo, sold it to a forum member. I Did all the work myself including the crossover pipe and all the mounting hardware.<P>Adrift- No, brakes were swaped with vented rotors at all 4 corners.<P>Rogue- The engine is a preformance rebuilt longblock from Jasper engines. All the intake had to be redone, I relocated the air filter and put it in the side scoop. That is a MSD BTM. The turbo is from a 86 T-bird, Garret t-3 .63 A/r. It's mounted with a spring loaded mount that's bolted to top of the tranny.<P>Terrybogin- I retained the stock ECM with the Stock Prom chip. I already had 19# injectors and a high flow fuel pump installed for My N2O. So I used a rising rate fuel pressure regulator to add more fuel under boost.<P>I'll put a list together of everything I used and total cost sometime. I know it was under $800, but I already had the Mig welder and my Bridgeport mill, and I couldn't imagin installing it with out one. <BR>I still need to fab up some heat shields and wrap some of the wires, and I'll be done, for now anyway||||reg||1
